    "title": "Little Rock puts special outreach policy in place for fireworks violations - NewsBreak",
    "text": "LITTLE ROCK, Ark. – Officials with the city of Little Rock are asking citizens to take special steps in reporting fireworks during celebrations surrounding Independence Day. Officials ask members of the community to use a special email address as fireworks complaints increase during the holiday. The address, LRPDFireworksViolations@LittleRock.gov will be monitored throughout the weekend, they said. Complaints sent to the address will receive an automated response, but will likely not receive contact from an officer, officials said. Police will respond to fireworks complaints alongside other responsibilities. Officials added that 911 should still be used for fireworks-related injuries or property damage, or to report gunfire. Non-emergency police reports can be made to 501-371-4829. The Little Rock Fire Department maintains a webpage on fireworks code and safety . According to the U.S. Consumer Product Safety Commission , nearly 15,000 Americans were injured by fireworks in 2024 and 11 people died. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KARK.",
